cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ANet4D in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ANet4D: Simulation Infrastructure for Collaborative Embodied Agents"
abstract: >-
  ANet4D is simulation infrastructure for collaborative embodied agents. It aims
  to be for collaborative embodied-agent research what NS-3 is for network
  research; its scope covers multi-UAV teams, unmanned ground and surface
  vehicles, ground robots, fixed sensors and software agents, and the released
  versions implement drones as the first entity class. It follows one chain,
  Reality to Reconstruction to World to Environment to Simulation to Agent:
  captured or reconstructed point clouds and photogrammetry meshes become
  versioned World Packages with geometry queries, an environment field adds
  wind, turbulence and visibility, a vectorised fleet simulator steps 1 to
  1,000 drones on one shared 250 Hz clock (real time at 1,000 drones on 0.53
  CPU core of an 8-vCPU Xeon E5-2603 v4 machine, median of 3 runs), and the
  Interactive Sandbox gives each visitor an isolated simulation core while the
  browser renders the world; its server needs no GPU. The Event Lab adds event
  tapes, Gazebo Sim lockstep, mesh-rendered camera, thermal and LiDAR sensors
  and a benchmark runtime; its sensor generation requires an NVIDIA GPU on the
  server. Drones discover each other's capabilities and delegate tasks through
  an in-process mock of the ANet network.
